+/* lenoxvi 0003 (2026-10-14): resend SCTP INIT until the association forms.
+ * Upstream raw SCTP sent exactly ONE INIT the instant DTLS completed, with
+ * no T1-init timer. Against aiortc (which is the PASSIVE SCTP side when we
+ * are ICE-controlling, and silently drops app data that lands before its
+ * SCTP transport registers — rtcdtlstransport.py `if self._data_receiver`)
+ * that lone INIT is lost on ~60% of sessions and the association never
+ * forms (bot: "Data channel not established within 10s"). Call every loop
+ * pass while CONNECTED; cheap no-op once connected. */
+void sctp_tick(Sctp* sctp);
